{:stage "PERCEIVE",
 :negative-controls
 {:planted-producers
  [{:id :reversed-error,
    :why
    "eps = mu - o. The sign of the miss is what R3 attributes by, so a reversed error moves belief the wrong way.",
    :verdict :caught,
    :caught-by [:eps-agrees-with-exact-reference]}
   {:id :precision-is-the-variance,
    :why
    "The registry's Pi is the RECIPROCAL of the floored variance. A producer that stamps the variance itself is confidently backwards.",
    :verdict :caught,
    :caught-by [:eps-agrees-with-exact-reference]}
   {:id :precision-without-the-floor,
    :why
    "1/v with no max. The eps0 floor is the whole content of the term at a certain likelihood.",
    :verdict :caught,
    :caught-by [:eps-agrees-with-exact-reference]}
   {:id :weighted-error-is-unweighted,
    :why
    "R3b's precision-weighted error dropped back to the raw error -- the failure that would make R7 inert without any error message.",
    :verdict :caught,
    :caught-by [:eps-agrees-with-exact-reference]}
   {:id :absent-observation-scored-as-zero,
    :why
    "The pre-AC1 producer: a channel this tick never observed scored against 0.0. Joe's 2026-09-02 ruling removed exactly this.",
    :verdict :caught,
    :caught-by [:eps-status-matches-declaration]}
   {:id :absence-dominates-refusal,
    :why
    "The order of the two guards reversed: an unobserved channel whose likelihood ALSO failed would be quietly omitted instead of refusing the whole update.",
    :verdict :caught,
    :caught-by [:eps-status-matches-declaration]}
   {:id :negative-variance-refused,
    :why
    "THE PLANT THAT LOOKS RIGHT. Refusing a negative predicted variance is what a reader would expect; the shipped producer scores it, because prediction-member checks finiteness and not sign (aif-equations.edn:83). The harness catches this plant, which is what makes the finding a fact about the shipped node rather than an opinion about it.",
    :verdict :caught,
    :caught-by
    [:eps-status-matches-declaration
     :eps-agrees-with-exact-reference
     :eps-refusal-names-offending-members]}
   {:id :contract-stamp-dropped,
    :why
    "A record with no producer contract cannot be told from a record written by a producer that predates the contract (C129).",
    :verdict :caught,
    :caught-by [:eps-contract-stamped]}
   {:id :f-pi-without-the-half,
    :why
    "The 1/2 dropped. Every candidate's F_pi doubles, and B.9 subtracts it from the policy score.",
    :verdict :caught,
    :caught-by [:f-pi-agrees-with-independent-association]}
   {:id :f-pi-log-variance-only,
    :why
    "ln(v) instead of ln(2 pi v): the Gaussian normaliser without its constant. Changes every total by a fixed per-channel offset, which a within-tick comparison would not reveal.",
    :verdict :caught,
    :caught-by [:f-pi-agrees-with-independent-association]}
   {:id :f-pi-residual-not-normalised,
    :why
    "r^2 instead of r^2/v. The channel with the least confident prediction would count most, not least.",
    :verdict :caught,
    :caught-by [:f-pi-agrees-with-independent-association]}
   {:id :f-pi-every-zero-floored,
    :why
    "The :floor arm applied to a BARE zero as well as to an action-model absent one -- the collapse the two-kinds-of-zero distinction exists to prevent.",
    :verdict :caught,
    :caught-by
    [:f-pi-branch-matches-declaration
     :f-pi-agrees-with-independent-association]}
   {:id :f-pi-negative-variance-scored,
    :why
    "A negative variance scored on its magnitude instead of rejected. Contrast the eps producer on the same node, which scores one -- the two rows do not agree, and that is a fact about R8, not about this plant.",
    :verdict :caught,
    :caught-by [:f-pi-branch-matches-declaration]}
   {:id :f-pi-skips-unmatched-channels,
    :why
    "Missing channels skipped instead of rejected -- a candidate scored on a subset of the evidence, which is how a partially-covered candidate would win a posterior it did not earn.",
    :verdict :caught,
    :caught-by [:f-pi-branch-matches-declaration]}],
  :n 14,
  :all-caught true,
  :reads
  "Each is a wrong R8 someone could write, and each must be caught by a check the SHIPPED producer passes. The two censuses below are excluded from that set, because they measure the node against a claim it does not meet and a check the shipped node fails cannot discriminate between a right producer and a wrong one."},
 :harness :v7-r8-node-sim,
 :f-pi
 {:fixtures
  [{:id :two-channel-positive,
    :why
    "The registry form, summed over two channels with different variances.",
    :expect :scored,
    :non-dyadic
    "ln(2 pi v) is transcendental; only the residual^2/v half is exact."}
   {:id :one-channel-zero-residual,
    :why
    "A perfect fit still costs the log-normaliser: F_pi is not zero when the residual is.",
    :expect :scored}
   {:id :absent-zero-floored,
    :why
    "PRODUCTION'S ARM. A zero the action model declared :absent carries no prediction; f-pi-dark-readback passes {:absent-variance :floor} (scripts/futon2/report/war_machine.clj:528-533), so the floor 0.01 is used.",
    :expect :scored,
    :non-dyadic "the 0.01 floor and the log."}
   {:id :absent-zero-rejects-by-default,
    :why
    "The function's OWN default is :reject. The same fixture rejects without the caller's declaration -- which is why the arm production takes had to be checked and not assumed.",
    :expect :rejected,
    :error :deterministic-mismatch}
   {:id :bare-zero-still-rejects-under-floor,
    :why
    "MachinePolicyFreeEnergyWitness.bareZeroStillRejectsUnderFloor: a zero with no :absent status is a real deterministic claim, and :floor does not rescue it.",
    :expect :rejected,
    :error :deterministic-mismatch}
   {:id :bare-zero-within-tolerance-contributes-nothing,
    :why
    "A deterministic claim the observation meets contributes 0.0 rather than an infinite density.",
    :expect :scored}
   {:id :zero-within-supplied-tolerance,
    :why
    ":deterministic-tolerance widens the band; the contribution is still exactly 0.0.",
    :expect :scored}
   {:id :negative-variance-rejects,
    :why
    "varianceTrichotomy's first arm: a negative variance always rejects. Contrast :present-negative-variance-scored above -- the eps producer on the SAME node scores one.",
    :expect :rejected,
    :error :invalid-variance}
   {:id :channel-mismatch-rejects,
    :why
    "Missing or extra channels are rejected rather than skipped or filled with zero (src/futon2/aif/policy_free_energy.clj:23-38).",
    :expect :rejected,
    :error :channel-mismatch}
   {:id :mixed-scored-and-deterministic,
    :why
    "One scored channel beside one absent-zero channel under :floor -- the shape a real tick takes, where 12 of 14 channels carry an action-model absent zero.",
    :expect :scored}],
  :fixture-count 10,
  :runs
  [{:fixture :two-channel-positive,
    :expect :scored,
    :status :scored,
    :error-key nil,
    :total 1.1731562955694275,
    :reference-total 1.1731562955694275,
    :scored-channels 2}
   {:fixture :one-channel-zero-residual,
